        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mikael Åkerfeldt, Lee Ranaldo, Steven Wilson\n- Bands and Projects: Opeth, Bloodbath, Steel, Storm Corrosion, Sonic Youth\n- Publications and Rankings: Rolling Stone, Greatest Guitarists of All Time\n- Roles: vocalist, guitarist, songwriter, singer-songwriter, writer, visual artist, record producer\n\nFacts:\n- Lee Ranaldo was born on February 3, 1956, and he is an American musician, singer-songwriter, guitarist, writer, visual artist, and record producer.\n- Mikael Åkerfeldt was born on 17 April 1974, and he is a Swedish musician.\n- Lee Ranaldo is best known as a co-founder of the alternative rock band Sonic Youth.\n- Mikael Åkerfeldt is the lead vocalist, guitarist, and primary songwriter of the progressive death metal band Opeth.\n- Mikael Åkerfeldt was the former vocalist of the death metal supergroup Bloodbath.\n- Mikael Åkerfeldt was also guitarist for the one-off band Steel.\n- Mikael Åkerfeldt is part of the collaboration Storm Corrosion with Steven Wilson.\n- In 2004, Rolling Stone ranked Lee Ranaldo number 33 on its Greatest Guitarists of All Time list.",
